{
  "id": "demo-mv-summer-pv",
  "name": "Vision MV – summer PV overvoltage",
  "description": "A midsummer week on the Vision MV network with high rooftop PV (about 125 % of each LV area's peak demand) and mostly sunny days, so the network exports power to the HV grid at midday. Look at the Violations tab and the voltage and loading views: LV busbars rise above 1.05 pu every sunny midday and the LS transformers are overloaded by reverse flow on the sunniest days. The network edits are deliberate: HV source at 1.03 pu, main transformer tap -1 and every LS transformer one tap step up (+2.4 %, the winter setting).",
